;; A vision appliance: a camera pipeline, an inference runtime with a carried
;; model, and a tunnel to send the result through.
;;
;; Four features from two packs, and none of them knows about the others.
;; gstreamer encodes, camera-stream sends to an address, inference runs a
;; model, wireguard is what that address routes through. Both packs carry an
;; overlay, and BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY takes both because Buildroot reads it as a
;; list — which Silt only learned when these two were first composed.
;;
;; Everything here runs on QEMU with no camera and no NPU: videotestsrc for
;; the source, tensorflow-lite on the CPU for the runtime. The RK3588 version
;; changes the target and the runtime symbol and nothing else.

(image qemu-arm-vision

  (compose
    target:qemu-aarch64-virt
    profile:standard
    feature:networking
    feature:gstreamer
    feature:camera-stream
    feature:inference)

  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
